From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: backport AR50_LITE support from 7.4

Every iris and venus commit between v7.3 and v7.4-rc4 that v7.3.5 does
not already carry, in upstream order, all in v7.4-rc1:

 8921f6da06fd media: venus: Drop session events without an instance
 452480931648 media: iris: cancel sys error work on driver removal
 6f4eb91fa276 Revert "media: iris: Add Gen2 firmware autodetect and fallback"
 a9ff61527805 media: iris: Add Gen2 firmware autodetect and fallback
 aaab46c331c2 media: iris: Skip UBWC configuration when not supported
 dc518127ff16 media: iris: drop IRIS_FMT_foo enumeration
 84663751b845 media: iris: Filter UBWC raw formats based on hardware capabilities
 0183b3f5505e media: iris: Introduce set_preset_register as a vpu_op
 35f2e53cdb63 media: iris: Introduce interrupt_init as a vpu_op
 f2a793f2f386 media: iris: add vpu op hook to disable ARP buffer
 2623cd6afd01 media: iris: Add platform data field for watchdog interrupt mask
 f3e7dc02ef40 media: iris: Add platform flag for instantaneous bandwidth voting
 857bc9c35eca media: iris: skip PIPE if it is not supported by the platform
 92b9674e4754 media: iris: Add framework support for AR50_LITE video core
 bfe9dfe9dd91 media: iris: add minimal GET_PROPERTY implementation
 d2375076b540 media: iris: update buffer requirements based on received info
 e53f8feb2e40 media: iris: implement support for the Agatti platform
 c60ced8bd1cd media: iris: Introduce buffer size calculations for AR50LT
 4278c4e87a2f media: iris: add Gen2 firmware support on the Agatti platform
 0016f9cbcf87 media: venus: skip QCM2290 if Iris driver is enabled
 49f9ad996ea5 media: iris: constify inst_fw_cap_sm8250_dec
 f301102c17f2 media: iris: fail firmware boot on invalid uc_region
 428e6f95e685 media: iris: take core lock when scanning the instance list
 95f9e9fc9336 media: iris: guard against a NULL hfi_sys_ops in the interrupt handler
 397ebadcbc21 media: iris: reject open() when the session limit is reached
 af5f7df6c8b3 media: iris: reference count video instances
 1237888922a7 media: iris: cache work mode after computing it in iris_set_stage
 a6ee1766b3db media: iris: force stage 1 work mode for CBR RC on encoder
 5f21cd9a4ae4 media: iris: add support for multi_slice in iris encoder
 89a3d2a2237e media: iris: fix 64-bit division in iris_set_slice_count()

They give iris the AR50_LITE core of QCM2290, which the SM6115 (through
its qcom,qcm2290-venus fallback) and the SM4450 (our video node) share,
with Gen1 (qcom/venus-6.0/venus.mbn) and Gen2
(qcom/vpu/ar50lt_p1_gen2_s6.mbn) firmware. With iris built, venus no
longer claims qcom,qcm2290-venus (0016f9cbcf87).

Not taken: 4dd10fbbeb9c (treewide devm_kmalloc_obj() conversion; 7.3
has no such API), so iris_probe.c and venus/core.c keep their 7.3
allocation calls. Seven others are in v7.3.5 already through stable.
With those two exceptions the iris and venus trees match v7.4-rc4.
All thirty cherry-pick onto v7.3.5 without conflicts.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
